node_modules/
dist/
.wrangler/
.env*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
*.log
coverage/

# worktrees (superpowers isolation)
.worktrees/

# REQ-167: client-side identity denylist never enters the repo
.identity-denylist.local

# Cloudflare Workers local secrets (RESEND_API_KEY, TEST_SEND_TOKEN, etc.) — never commit
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
**/.dev.vars

# build artifacts regenerated from pinned hashes
seed/SEED-1.json
tools/design/report.json

# release/merge evidence records (REQ-288) — generated per run, never committed
artifacts/

# Playwright advisory harness output (perf + screenshot diff) — never committed
test-results/
playwright-report/
tests/visual/blessed/*-diff.png
tests/visual/blessed/*-actual.png

# macOS/iCloud name-collision duplicates (see WP-06 session note) — never commit these.
# Broadened 2026-08-05 (audit §253): the rules covered ONLY " 2", but macOS mints " 3", " 4", … on every
# subsequent collision, so `0008_x 3.sql` was committable — a tracked duplicate migration would corrupt the
# forward-only lock and the schema itself. Character classes cover 2–99.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9][0-9].*
*\ [0-9].*
*\ [0-9][0-9].*

# Operator-supplied preflight state (account-side facts). Named at the repo root by
# docs/ops/LAUNCH-RUNBOOK.md Step 3 — it asserts what is bound in a live account and is never committed.
*-state.json

# Per-session loop state written by the ralph-loop plugin (iteration counter, session id) —
# transient machine state; a bulk `git add` of the untracked set must never sweep it in (2026-08-01 audit).
.claude/ralph-loop.local.md

# Editor-generated agent-instruction packs (VS Code Mermaid extension "Install AI Skills" etc.) —
# vendor tooling, referenced by nothing tracked; committing them would make them repo-wide agent
# instructions nobody reviewed (2026-08-01 audit). Author real instructions deliberately if ever wanted.
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.github/instructions/
